            "By modern measure, this is about 1 degree, 36 minutes, and 25 seconds, or just over 1.5 degrees. [...] "
            "Due to the limited width of the card, the kamal was only really useful for measuring Polaris in equatorial latitudes, where Polaris remains close to the horizon. "
            "This fact may explain why it was not common in Europe.",
